  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tresillo. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tresillo (also Rocambor) is a historic Spanish trick-taking game for three players. It is the Spanish descendant of L'Hombre (Ombre), which was once the most popular card game in Europe. The 'declarer' (El Hombre) plays alone against the other two. Uses a 40-card Spanish deck with the unusual A-3-K ranking.",
    objective: 'Declarer must win more tricks than either opponent.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal 9. 2. Bid (Normal, Vuelta, Solo). Highest bid becomes Declarer. 3. Declarer discards and draws from stock. Opponents may also draw. 4. Play 9 tricks. Follow suit. Trumps beat plain. 5. Declarer wins if taking 5+ tricks (against 2 opponents).',
